# --- the field corpus -------------------------------------------------------
# trazo4 is unpublished and has no accompanying peer-reviewed publication. It must not
# leave this machine. Never commit, never push to a public bucket. Regenerate with
# pipeline/repack_fields.py from E:\trazo4_fields_parquet.
data/fields/
data/inventory.json

# The ten public example windows are a deliberate, authorised subset of that corpus and
# DO ship, but only from docs/ - the build output. These are the working copies.
data/response/fields_*.geojson

# Per-field trend series are copied verbatim into docs/ by the build, so committing the
# working copy too would store every byte twice. The response_*.json files are NOT
# duplicates - they keep the full per-field table the published copy strips out, which is
# what lets the site be rebuilt without re-pulling Sentinel-2.
data/response/series_*.json

# --- the CHIRPS drought pipeline, in drought/ -------------------------------
# All reproducible by running the pipeline: CHIRPS rasters, the basin product, the
# catalogue. About 830 MB.
drought/data/
drought/output/
drought/catalog/

# --- build and run artefacts ------------------------------------------------
# Vendored MapLibre: ignored at the root, where it is refetchable, but docs/vendor/ IS
# committed - the published site cannot load it from a CDN, because MapLibre tiles GeoJSON
# in a web worker and a cross-origin script cannot spawn one.
/vendor/

# Scratch build target used to smoke-test the site assembly.
docs_test/

*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
